      "derived": "Ningbo Kangnex WJ128V-5.0-04P screw terminal block (LCSC C192769; customer drawing WJ128V-5.0-XXP-1Y-00A, version A, 2024.03.10, in the LCSC PDF, read 2026-10-04): 4 poles at 5.00 mm, pins 0.90 x 0.80, PCB holes 1.50, body 20.00 x 10.28 with the pin row 4.90 from the back face and so 5.38 from the wire-entry face, a 0.60 lug at one end. No stock horizontal 4-pole footprint at 5.00 mm has 1.5 mm holes (they have 1.1 to 1.4) or this body. Edits to Phoenix's MKDS 1,5 block (holes 1.3 in 2.6 mm pads; body 5.2 behind and 4.6 in front of the pin row): holes 1.5 mm in 2.8 mm pads (the same 0.65 mm ring); what lies in front of the pin row moves 0.78 mm out with the wire-entry face and what lies behind it 0.3 mm in with the back face (body, silkscreen, courtyard, texts); 0.6 mm more courtyard at pin 1's end for the lug. The 3D model is still Phoenix's block, a stand-in."
